This project measures a resource-cost property of the SQIsign reference
implementation. It contains NO cryptographic code of its own and vendors no
upstream source. It drives an external verify-timing adapter and, to build
that adapter and to obtain honest test vectors, refers to the upstream project:

  Upstream: The SQIsign team, "SQIsign" reference implementation
  Commit:   dd133d7aca576c361a270c8e6434832535b42ecc
  License:  Apache License 2.0 (portions LGPL, see upstream COPYING.LGPL)
  URL:      https://github.com/SQIsign/the-sqisign

Test vectors (Known Answer Test .rsp files) used to obtain honest, verifying
signatures are produced by that upstream project. The results committed in
this repository were derived by measuring against an adapter built from that
commit. The relevant KAT files and their SHA-256 digests (as measured this
session) are:

  PQCsignKAT_353_SQIsign_lvl1.rsp
    03898a4b415c0fd038137b1e5716be07ea7641622161aef0777035a96fc9bba8
  PQCsignKAT_529_SQIsign_lvl3.rsp
    073b6fa0e7792267965306f8cccded420b9c2d4719d49295d31041c194fd9526
  PQCsignKAT_701_SQIsign_lvl5.rsp
    2509ecc191791385968a36db50d8479c87d3e1b8bd655150f927f1f5613f2546

No KAT files, upstream source, or cryptographic key material are redistributed
in this repository. Only measurement results (timings and amplification
factors) derived from them are committed.

The classical-signature baselines were measured with OpenSSL 3.6.3 (9 Jun 2026).
